# kex: check-only
# A `params:` entry whose type half is not parseable Kex is a clean compile
# error at the Template.text call site — not a crash. (A genuinely
# unparseable type once reached an uncaught exception from deep inside the
# parser: Parser::error() records a diagnostic and then throws, which is
# fine for parseProgram's own recovery loop and was not fine for a bare
# parseTypeExpr() call with no such loop above it.)

main do
  let show = Template.text(`---
params: [count: ->->->]
---
<%= count %>`)
  IO.printLine(show(1))
end
